 \"1956\"]. Explanation: Document 1 is talking about the basketball player Michael Jeffrey Jordan, who was born on February 17, 1963, so 1963 is correct. Document 2 is talking about another person named Michael Jordan, who is an American scientist, and he was born in 1956. Therefore, the answer 1956 from Document 2 is also correct. Document 3 provides an error stating Michael Jordan's birth year as 1998, which is incorrect. Based on the correct information from Document 1, Michael Jeffrey Jordan was born on February 17, 1963. Document 4 does not provide any useful information.\n\nQuestion: Who is the director of the Assassin's Creed movie?\nDocument 1: Aymar Azaïzia, head of Assassin's Creed content at Ubisoft, stated that the film, which is \"a brand new story, [with] new characters set in our universe\", had ...\nDocument 2: Dec 19, 2016 ... Assassin's Creed, the first film to spin out of Ubisoft's popular action/adventure franchise, has high aspirations. Director Justin Kurzel ...\nDocument 3: Dec 19, 2016 ... Assassin's Creed, the first film to spin out of Ubisoft's popular action/adventure franchise, has high aspirations. Director James Cameron ...\n\nAdditional extracted evidence from the SAME documents (not independent sources and not guaranteed true). Use alongside the original documents above.\n[{\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"card_id\": \"d2:c0\", \"entity\": \"Justin Kurzel\", \"scope\": \"Director of the Assassin's Creed movie\", \"claim\": \"The director of the Assassin's Creed movie is Justin Kurzel.\", \"answer\": \"Justin Kurzel\", \"quote\": \"Director Justin Kurzel ...\", \"original_document_number\": 2}]\nRAMDocs final output contract (overrides example output formats): Return JSON with accepted_answers (all correct SHORT answer strings, including multiple valid answers; empty list if unsupported) and explanation (reasoning). Do not put confidence, sources or explanatory sentences in accepted_answers."
